# Each trial/run materializes its own git repo under runs/**/repo/ (its own
# .git, its own history) so it never touches this repo's. Committing a
# nested .git would make it a gitlink, not a normal tree — never do that.
# The evidence that matters (prompt, transcript, diff, commit subjects,
# verdict) is written as plain files alongside repo/ and IS committed.
runs/**/repo/
